.hooks/repo-cfg.sh
# DO NOT re-add "package-lock.json" here. Every tracked package.json in this repo must
# have a tracked package-lock.json beside it. A package.json records what was ASKED for;
# only the lock records what was actually resolved, and every directory here is a
# PUBLISHED npm package -- so a lock nobody can see is a tree nobody can review.
#
# @prescient-devices/mssql-client shipped a total outage exactly this way: its
# node_modules held util 1.18.1 while its own lock already pinned 1.26.5, util 1.20.6
# renamed RetryMngr's `args` to `funcArgs` in a PATCH bump, and every query() rejected
# before any SQL reached the server, for months. The lock was gitignored, so the tree it
# ran against and the tree it claimed to run against were never compared by anything.
#
# Locks inside node_modules/ stay ignored: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded. That is the intended scope.
.npmrc
node_modules/
